Revision history for Pakku

chou  2026-10-07

  The ecosystem release. recman.pakku.org is gone; Pakku now lives where the dists live.

  Ecosystems
    - fez (https://360.zef.pm) is the recommendation manager, the Raku Ecosystem Archive
      (REA) answers when fez has nothing, and is only loaded then. Both indexes are kept under
      ~/.pakku/.index and refreshed when stale (fez 1 h, rea 24 h), on `pakku refresh`, or once
      when a dist is missing from an index older than ten minutes. `norefresh` keeps Pakku off
      the network. `pakku nuke index` forgets every index.
    - Resolution, search and info are local: no server round trips, newest release first,
      versions honoured by local recmans too.
    - HTTPS through a NativeCall libcurl binding, with the curl or wget binary as fallback
      (curl.exe on Windows). Pakku::HTTP and the recman.pakku.org protocol are gone; an old
      config entry is ignored with a hint to run `pakku config recman reset`.
    - fez tarballs are verified against the SHA-1 in their name when a sha1 tool is around.

  Specs (S11 / S22)
    - `<...>` adverbs are strings with Raku's rules (ver<1.2> is a prefix, ver<1.2+>, ver<1.*>,
      auth<zef:*>); `(...)` adverbs are smartmatch selectors evaluated by Raku: ranges,
      junctions, regexes, Whatever code, Any; numbers inside ver( ) and api( ) are versions.
      Selectors are data, never code (no blocks, calls or variables): a spec also comes from
      other people's META files. Installed dists are matched by Rakudo's own candidates().
    - META `depends` in every S22 form: hash form (name/ver/auth/api/from/hints, adverbs inside
      name), `any` alternatives (first one the recman can serve wins), phased
      runtime/build/test x requires/recommends/suggests (requires are the hard ones),
      by-env / by-env-exists / by-distro / by-kernel / by-raku / by-vm switches with Version
      keys (+ / - suffixes), legacy build-depends / test-depends lists and hashes,
      :from<bin>, :from<native>, :from<Perl5>. Unknown `from` values die instead of returning False.

  Commands
    - `pakku refresh [recman ...]` (rfr), general options `refresh` / `norefresh` (nrfr).
    - `pakku info dist` (i): newest release, every release by author, what is installed where,
      who depends on it.
    - `pakku add ./dist-1.0.tar.gz`, `pakku add https://host/dist.tar.gz`,
      `pakku add https://host/user/dist.git#tag` (git, also #branch / #sha); the same sources
      work for `test` and `build`.
    - `pakku search` defaults to `latest` (one row per dist and author) and `relaxed`;
      `nolatest` shows every release; search errors reach the exit code.
    - `pakku test timeout <sec>`, `pakku build timeout <sec>`: a child quiet for that long is
      killed (default 420, 0 never); the clock starts with the process, silent processes count.
    - `pakku nuke index`; `nuke home|site|vendor` remove only the repo directories;
      `nuke core` is documented and needs force.
    - A path add warns about lib/ modules missing from provides (issue #36).

  Fixes
    - Archive extraction validates every entry (no absolute paths, .., links or device files,
      nothing outside the dist root), streams data instead of trusting declared sizes, checks
      every libarchive return value and removes half extracted dists.
    - Dependency resolution: one visited set per run, `exclude` by name, a spec satisfied by a
      dist chosen earlier in the same run (one Foo for Foo:ver<0.2+> and a bare Foo),
      recommends/suggests are no longer hard requirements, Int apis match, leading `v` versions
      match and sort, `any` groups after the first are not dropped.
    - Builders get their META as JSON (the .raku literal was parsed as a block, every dist with
      a `builder` failed to build).
    - `pakku update` no longer removes another author's dist of the same name; an installed
      dist without api is not an update every time.
    - yolo works inside parallel fetches; errors exit 1 after cleaning .tmp / .stage; a failing
      test stops further tests from starting; symlinks are never followed or copied.
    - Command line: `notest Foo` / `nt Foo` / `nb Foo` no longer run test / build, `add p`,
      `help state`, malformed config commands are rejected, unknown commands and options exit 1
      with a hint instead of printing the help with -Ofun.
    - Config: values keep their type (Int, Bool, list); recman entries are validated as a whole
      (type ecosystem|local, mirrors, index, source, refresh, priority); reset of a module
      without a default removes it; config.json is written 0600 and mirror credentials are
      redacted in logs; `comment-*-delimit` keys work.
    - Environment: command options under their command (PAKKU_ADD_TO works), booleans parse
      true/false/yes/no/on/off, PAKKU_CACHE takes true/false or a path, PAKKU_SEARCH_COUNT,
      PAKKU_REFRESH, PAKKU_TEST_TIMEOUT, PAKKU_BUILD_TIMEOUT.
    - `pakku list repo <path>` lists that repo, `dont download` works, `add to` / `contained`
      decide "already added" against the target repo, build logs BLD.
    - Pakku loads on hosts without libarchive or libcurl (native libraries are resolved when
      used, with a hint when missing); dlopen uses RTLD_NOW only.

  Internals
    - Pakku::Util, Pakku::Fetch, Pakku::Curl, Pakku::Collapse, Pakku::Recman::Index,
      Pakku::Recman::Ecosystem, Pakku::Command::Refresh, Pakku::Command::Info are new;
      Pakku::HTTP and Pakku::Recman::HTTP are gone. The commands share the core's resolve,
      fetch, stage and deploy helpers (about 900 lines of copies removed).
    - Offline test suite with a fixture ecosystem (index, tarballs, crafted evil archives) and
      an optional network test (PAKKU_TEST_NETWORK=1); CI runs the suite on Rakudo 2025.06 and
      latest and installs a fez dist and a REA-only dist.

celastrina.6  2026-10-06

  - The last release against recman.pakku.org.
